<title>FRANCE: US tops Paris airports export destinations in May.</title>
<headline>US tops Paris airports export destinations in May.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. was the main destination for export traffic from the Paris airports in May 1997, the airport authority, (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>May 1997 export traffic via Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 48,569 tonnes, an increase of 4.3 percent on the same period last year,it added.</p>
<p>The 20 top May destinations with percentage change on May 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p>	Origin	    tonnes    Percent</p>
<p>					  Change 1996</p>
<p>    1. United States  10,867    up  6.0</p>
<p>    2. Japan	     2,344    up  1.1</p>
<p>    3. Hong Kong	 2,249    up 25.1</p>
<p>    4. Germany	   2,015    up 22.3</p>
<p>    5. Britain	   1,652    up 18.4</p>
<p>    6. Canada	    1,564  down  9.9</p>
<p>    7. U.A.E.	    1,430    up  2.3</p>
<p>    8. India	     1,160    up 10.0</p>
<p>    9. Mexico	    1,130    up 26.4</p>
<p>   10. Brazil		980  down 17.6</p>
<p>   11. Fr.W.Indies	 934  down  4.4</p>
<p>   12. Singapore	   905    up 33.8</p>
<p>   13. Reunion	     851  down  4.3</p>
<p>   14. China		 760    up 13.4</p>
<p>   15. Saudia Arabia     756    up 12.5</p>
<p>   16. Egypt		 697  down  6.1</p>
<p>   17. Korea		 667  down  3.1</p>
<p>   18. Italy		 657  down  5.1</p>
<p>   19. Lebanon	     611  down  3.5</p>
<p>   20. Spain &amp; Canaries  581    up 25.8</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
